<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10163" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conflictĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		confligo (mostly in Cic. and Quint.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a striking together, a collision.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">duorum inter se corporum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					3, 6, 6</span></i>
			.—Esp., <i>a conflict, combat</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">totius exercitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
				7</span></i>
			 (6), 3, 1.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a contest,
			conflict</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rerum contrariarum et dissimilium et inter se
					pugnantium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Part. Or. 16, 55</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">29, 102</span></i>; <i><span class="en">30, 104</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 3, 6,
				4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 6,
			11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 1,
			18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
